The fallback console path candidates resolved from `__dirname` are off by a couple directories: from `packages/cli/src/commands` (and also from the built `dist/commands`), `../../apps/console` and `../../../apps/console` will never reach the monorepo root. This makes the “relative path from packages/cli” lookup ineffective and can cause `objectui studio` to fail unless run from the repo root. Update the candidate list to include the correct number of `..` segments (or compute the workspace root explicitly) so the lookup works as intended.
```suggestion
  // 1. Check monorepo structure from current working directory (apps/console)
  // 2. Check monorepo root relative to this file (packages/cli/src/commands -> ../../../..)
  const monorepoRootFromCli = resolve(__dirname, '../../../../');
  const candidates = [
    join(cwd, 'apps/console'),
    join(monorepoRootFromCli, 'apps/console'),
```
